---
import SectionHeading from './SectionHeading.astro';
import Shot from './Shot.astro';
---

<section id="pull-requests" class="px-4 sm:px-6 py-20" aria-labelledby="pull-requests-heading">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
    <SectionHeading id="pull-requests-heading" lead="Pull requests, next to your code." detail="Review, create, and follow stacks without leaving the repository." />

    <div class="tile-grid tile-grid-split mt-12">
      <article class="tile">
        <div class="tile-stage has-shot">
          <Shot name="pulls" alt="The pull request list with check status, changed lines, and stack layer indicators such as 2/3." />
        </div>
        <div class="tile-copy">
          <h3>Review without switching apps.</h3>
          <p>Read descriptions, checks, commits, and full or per-commit diffs. Create a pull request from your branch.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="tile">
        <div class="tile-stage has-shot">
          <Shot name="stack" alt="Pull request #24 with its stack indicator open, listing the three layers of stack #3 above main." />
        </div>
        <div class="tile-copy">
          <h3>Follow native stacks.</h3>
          <p>A layer indicator such as 2/3 shows where a pull request sits in its GitHub stack. Open it to reach the other layers.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Uses the GitHub CLI (<code class="font-mono text-foreground">gh</code>), signed in on the machine running OpenTig. <a href="/docs/github/" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground">GitHub and pull requests guide</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
